@@ -1,5 +1,7 @@
 # AI Changelog
 
+- **Projects redesign, faithful re-port of the approved demo (branch `redesign/projects-ops-console`, not deployed):** replaced the first port's minimal "terminal decorations on the old structure" with a faithful copy of the demo's design tokens and layout: demo palette (burnt-orange accent, teal/green/amber badges, `#eef1f5` light / `#080d15` dark backgrounds, dark terminal panels), Be Vietnam Pro + JetBrains Mono loaded as `--font-demo-sans` / `--font-demo-mono` alongside the existing Inter / Geist Mono imports, and the demo's dense section rhythm (26px section padding, numbered `01–…` section headings). List page: terminal hero with prompt line, headline, lead and a 4-cell stats grid computed from real data (case-study count, 3 environments, technology count, architecture-diagram count); toolbar with count + filters reordered to All / Production / AWS / Kubernetes / DevOps / Lab; cards rebuilt to the demo structure (outlined index number, type + status badges, kind line, ▸ highlights, computed fact chips for phases / technologies / architecture planes, teal tags, "View case study →" button + status footnote) plus the demo's Lab/Design footnote. Detail pages: dot-brand header, pill subnav (not sticky), 6-cell meta grid (Role, Timeline, Type/Status, Infrastructure, Repository as owner/repo path, Original), Problem split into Constraints / Success-criteria panels, architecture planes + architecture SVGs on the demo's dark diagram figure (the SVGs are dark-themed), phases as numbered circles with Tools / Output chips, decisions table, Security & Observability merged into one two-panel section with both anchors preserved, Results as tick list, Challenges as stacked cards with Approach / Lesson blocks, actions moved to a bottom button row, pagination as buttons, and a demo-style site footer. Deliberate deviations from the demo, all from repo constraints: content stays English (demo is Vietnamese); card fact chips are computed from structured fields (no per-project hardcoded numbers); badges derive from type + status fields (the demo's editorial "Lab" badge on Banking / "Production-oriented" on Datxe are not in structured data); the demo's hand-drawn SVG data-flow diagrams and per-project "honest" boxes stay out (no data field for them); the demo's `prefers-color-scheme` dark mode is implemented through the repo's `html.dark` ThemeToggle mechanism with the same dark palette. Presentation-only: no Payload schema, migration, seed, CMS record, media object, or production data write was performed. Not pushed; review on the branch first.
+
 - **Projects ops-console redesign (branch `redesign/projects-ops-console`, not deployed):** restyled the project portfolio list and detail pages to the approved ops-console design without changing project content, routes, Payload schema, or deployment scripts. The list hero gains a terminal-style project index rendered from real project fields, and the alternating timeline becomes a two-column case-study card grid with a terminal header bar per card. Filters are now All / AWS / Kubernetes / DevOps / Lab / Production, mapped to category, type (Lab), and status (Production = completed), with a live result count; the previous Linux / Terraform / Observability filters were removed. Detail pages gain a terminal-style hero bar and a sticky anchor subnav (Problem, Architecture, Implementation, Decisions, Security, Observability, Results, Challenges, Gallery) that only lists sections the project actually has; all sections, metadata, JSON-LD, prev/next navigation, and architecture SVGs are unchanged. Presentation-only: no Payload schema, migration, seed, CMS record, media object, or production data write was performed. Not pushed; review on the branch first.
 
 - **Production project replacement migration:** added a one-time, backup-first Payload migration that replaces the existing project records with the six published source projects, verifies the final published slug set, and uses `overrideAccess` server-side because the collection is intentionally read-only through the admin API. The migration is pending production deployment; no production project record was changed by this code change.
